+      <div><p class="chapter">QUESTIONS, ANSWERED</p><h2>the small print,<br>at normal size.</h2></div>
+      <div class="faq__list">
+        <details open><summary>Why does Android show an installation warning?</summary><p>The APK is distributed directly rather than through Google Play. Confirm the domain is berthalla.io and compare the SHA-256 above before installing.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Does it connect to my wallet?</summary><p>No. There is no wallet connection, signing, trading or account flow. Market tools and widgets provide informational data; the app cannot move funds.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Can I make and save cards offline?</summary><p>Yes. Caption cards are made on your device and saved in the app’s private collection. You can reopen them offline. Sharing exports a PNG to the recipient app you select. Cards are not backed up to a Berthalla account; uninstalling BERT removes its private collection.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Where are my BERT holdings stored?</summary><p>Only in the app’s private storage on your device. Your entered amount and optional total cost are used locally for estimated values. Neither is sent to Berthalla or a third party.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>How often does market data refresh?</summary><p>The app requests a background refresh every 15 minutes. Android ultimately controls scheduling and may delay work to preserve battery. The widget shows the quote age and marks delayed data.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>How do updates work?</summary><p>Return to this page for new releases. Download the newer APK and install it over the existing app; keep the existing app installed to preserve its private data.</p></details>
+        <details><summary>Is there an iPhone version?</summary><p>Not yet. BERT is currently available for Android 8.0 and newer.</p></details>
